{title: Forgive Me}
{lyricist: Sergio Rykov}
{composer: Sergio Rykov}

{start_of_verse}
Who are you to me - a friend or just someone I know?
I remember your gaze, that burning gaze
That painfully twisted your face,
A silhouette slipping out of my hands.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Who? You. To me. Isn't it clear?
Don't you feel the falseness and the growing coldness,
This burning emptiness and distance,
In my "It's all fine, don't wo-o-orry".
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Who are you to me? Like a mantra stuck in my head -
Nonsense, creeping in and in, winding me up.
I can no longer tell where the truth is and where
I made it up myself and then believed it myself.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Who? To me? I don't care anymore,
But why then can't I fall asleep?
Why do myriads of thoughts and phrases
Swarm and repeat themselves in every way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Who are you to me? And who is saying this to me?
What is this voice inside that keeps on repeating,
Locking inside itself all of my pa-a-a-a-ain,
Not giving it away and not sharing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Who am I then? Why can't I see myself?
Only a sniffling nose is heard in the silence.
Only the trembling of shoulders from a silent scream.
Only a downcast gaze from within.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Why does it hurt so much? Oh God!
It aches - my heart, alive and trembling.
Tender, gentle, vulnerable.
Endlessly open and so warm.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
A sigh. Deep, with relief.
Shoulders straighten, the gaze lifts.
An old trauma, again, almost, probably.
It makes me stir up the poison.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
What? Am I. Doing. Why?
Why am I breaking into a thousand pieces
Our bond - many-sided, cast
By hours of our talks and meetings.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Love. It seems that is what I forgot,
Going deep into myself in the moment.
Into my pain, forgetting about you.
A sigh. A breath. Easier.
{end_of_verse}
